course: dictionary
lesson: 5392
title: Short words, big meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: KO is a short word, and it is an abbreviation for «knockout». In boxing, a KO means one fighter has been hit so hard they cannot get up, so the fight is over.
explain: Context gives you clues. On a game screen, «K.O.!» shows that a character has been beaten. In sports news, «win by KO» means the fight ended with a knockout.
explain: Slang can change the meaning. «I was totally KO'd» means I was very tired, as if I had been knocked out. Ko is also a surname, for example in Korea and China, so a capital letter inside a name is not a fight word.
fact: KO is short for «knockout».
fact: KO is an abbreviation, so it stands for a longer word. It is usually written in capitals.
fact: «I was totally KO'd» is informal slang and means very tired.
fact: In Ilo, -ko turns a doing word into the person who does it: dami (to run), damiko (runner). This -ko is an ending, not the word KO.
fact: In French, «le chocolat» is «luh sho-ko-LA», so the middle syllable sounds like the word KO.
exercise: In boxing, what does «KO» mean? | A referee's whistle | A kiss on the cheek | A new pair of gloves | *The fight ends because one fighter is knocked out
exercise: «I was totally KO'd after the match.» What does KO'd suggest? | *Very tired, as if knocked out | Very wet | Very hungry | Very excited
exercise: In «luh sho-ko-LA», which part sounds like the word KO? | sho | luh | *ko | LA
test: In Ilo, «dami» means to run. What does «damiko» mean? | A race | To sing | A running shoe | *A runner
test: On a game screen the words «K.O.!» appear. What does this tell you? | A new level is ready | The player has won a prize | The game has just started | *A character has been beaten
exam: KO is short for which word? | keep-out | *knockout | kick-on | knock-off
